# Provenance for jxl_encode_mem_2026-06-23.tsv
commit_jxl_encoder_main_at_sweep: 1cf97d18
host: lilith (WSL2, AMD Ryzen 9, 28 cores)
date: 2026-06-23
probe: zenjxl examples/mem_probe_encode (threads-arg variant), built --features parallel
  args: <rgb8.bin> <w> <h> <lossy|lossless> <effort> <quality> [threads] [est]
measure: VmHWM marginal = peak-RSS delta around encode() = encoder MARGINAL working set
  (excludes binary floor + caller input buffer); one process per cell.
env: GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.mmap_threshold=131072 (WSL2 glibc-arena RSS stability)
fit: scripts/mem_peak_fit.py shape (marginal = alpha + beta*pixels per band, OLS across sizes);
  band const = smallest linear upper bound clearing MAX measured at every size with >=10% margin.
purpose: recalibrate src/heuristics.rs estimate_encode (the 2026-06-14 1024-only fit conflated
  alpha into beta -> TYP behaved like MAX; 4.16x over on lossy buttloop, UNDER on lossless e6).
columns: w h pixels mode effort quality threads content out_bytes pre_rss_kb vmhwm_kb marginal_kb
  (12MP rows: pre/vmhwm zeroed, marginal_kb from direct measurement)
